+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Shipped              |
+
+This spec defines the input-validation contract for tool calls; its `Status` records test citation coverage rather than implementation progress.
+
+## Registry contract
+
+- `ToolRegistry.execute` rejects missing required fields, wrong types, and values outside an enum before invoking the executor; it returns a `ToolResponse` whose result identifies the failing property path and constraint without disclosing the offending value, log lines also omit that value, valid input including unknown extra properties reaches the executor unchanged exactly once, and an unknown tool name still throws `Unknown tool: <name>` ([validated by: rejects invalid input without executing or disclosing values, and passes valid input through unchanged](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L17)).
+- A static schema is compiled at registration, so an uncompilable schema throws then with the tool's name, and ten later calls reuse the schema compiled at registration ([validated by: rejects an uncompilable static schema at registration and reuses a compiled static schema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L63)).
+- A function-valued tool definition is resolved for each call, and that call's input is validated against the schema returned then rather than a schema from an earlier call ([validated by: validates each call against a function definition’s current schema](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L98)).
+
+## Conversation contract
+
+- A rejected tool call is returned to the model as a tool result; the model can correct and retry it in a later round within the existing tool-round limit, and `processMessage` resolves normally after the corrected call ([validated by: returns a schema rejection to the model so it can correct the tool call in the next round](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L7)).
